Relicensing
-----------

MIT is compatible with GPL-3.0 in one direction: MIT-licensed code may be
incorporated into a GPL-3.0 work, and the combined work is then distributed
under the GPL-3.0. `changi` is GPL-3.0, so the ported code is distributed under
GPL-3.0 while this notice preserves the original copyright and permission
notice, as the MIT licence requires.

The conversion is ONE-WAY. Nothing in `src/puff/` may be copied back into an
MIT-licensed project on the strength of its origin here, and no part of the
rest of `changi` becomes MIT-licensed by being adjacent to it.
